{#- modules/verifiers/decision-models.j2
    Decision models (System One models): what comes back, and how fast.

    Both slides are built from the Zenable "Decision models" lab on main
    (services/ui_frontend labs/decision-models.mdx, October 2026): one support
    ticket sent to a chat model held to a JSON enum and to Jev asked a Choice,
    then the lab's 30-ticket benchmark of Jev and Claude Haiku 5.5 on accuracy,
    latency, cost and calibration. Those numbers are the lab's own output,
    unchanged. The Claude Opus 5.5 row was measured separately on the same 30
    tickets through the Claude API (claude -p, effort low, 27 October 2026);
    the footnote on the slide says so.

    Written against the brand-pack primitive contract (see AGENTS.md): colours
    come from the engine's --slide-* and --accent-* tokens, so light mode and
    other packs need nothing extra. Import WITH CONTEXT:

      {%- from "modules/verifiers/decision-models.j2" import
          probability_not_prose, speed with context %}
-#}

{%- from "modules/branding/" ~ branding ~ "/primitives.j2" import
    content_slide,
    slide_heading
-%}

{%- set _STYLE %}
<style>
  .dm { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 28px; margin: 8px 0 18px; }
  .dm-ask { font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.4; color: var(--slide-ink-2); margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .dm-ask strong { color: var(--slide-ink); }
  .dm-k { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--slide-ink-3); margin: 0 0 8px; }
  .dm-k.on { color: var(--accent-success); }
  .dm-code { margin: 0; padding: 16px 18px; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--slide-sunken); border: 1px solid var(--slide-hairline); color: var(--slide-ink); font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.45; white-space: pre; }
  .dm-note { font-size: 17px; color: var(--slide-ink-2); margin: 10px 0 0; }
  .dm-src { font-size: 11px; color: var(--slide-ink-3); margin: 10px 0 0; text-align: right; }
  .dms { width: 100%; max-height: 48vh; display: block; margin: 6px 0 10px; }
  .dms text { fill: var(--slide-ink); font-size: 26px; font-weight: 700; }
  .dms .sub { fill: var(--slide-ink-2); font-size: 17px; font-weight: 500; }
  .dms .sub .sep { fill: var(--slide-ink-3); }
  .dms .ms { font-size: 26px; }
  .dms .axis { stroke: var(--slide-rule); stroke-width: 1; }
  .dms .jev { fill: var(--accent-success); }
  .dms .haiku { fill: var(--accent-info); }
  .dms .opus { fill: var(--accent-warning); }
  .dms .p95 { opacity: 0.35; }
  .dms .legend { fill: var(--slide-ink-3); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 400; }
</style>
{%- endset %}


{%- macro probability_not_prose() -%}
{%- call content_slide("Decision model output") %}
  {{ _STYLE }}
  {{ slide_heading("", "Probability, not prose",
                   "A System One model answers a question with a probability per option. A chat model held to a schema answers with a label.") }}
  <p class="dm-ask"><strong>Ticket:</strong> &ldquo;Hi. Long story. We migrated our SSO from Okta to Entra in March, everything worked, then in April we added a second domain, which also worked. Last week our admin rotated the signing certificate per your docs and now every user who logs in sees a blank white page after the redirect. Sorry for the essay. Can you check your side?&rdquo; &nbsp;<strong>Which department?</strong> account &middot; billing &middot; sales &middot; technical</p>
  <div class="dm">
    <div>
      <p class="dm-k">Chat model, held to a JSON enum</p>
<pre class="dm-code">{
  "department": "technical"
}</pre>
      <p class="dm-note">A valid label. Nothing to threshold, and nothing to measure calibration with.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="dm-k on">Decision model, asked a Choice</p>
<pre class="dm-code">{
  "choice": "technical",
  "confidence": 0.35,
  "probabilities": {
    "account":   0.49,
    "billing":   0.00,
    "sales":     0.00,
    "technical": 0.51
  }
}</pre>
      <p class="dm-note">p(technical) = 0.51. Below a 0.90 floor nobody touches the SSO config on autopilot: a person looks first.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="dm-src">Jev 1.14 (198 ms) and Claude Haiku 5.5 (1,284 ms). Sources: docs.typesafe.ai &middot; artificialanalysis.ai/methodology/decision-index</p>
{%- endcall %}
{%- endmacro -%}


{%- macro speed() -%}
{#- Bars share one scale: the slowest p95 spans 900 px, so its label still fits.
    The darker bar is the median, the pale extension runs out to p95.
    (cls, name, p50, p95, [facts]) -#}
{%- set rows = [
  ("jev",   "Jev 1.14",          159,  224, ["29/30 correct", "$0.0006 for 30", "calibration error (Brier) 0.022"]),
  ("haiku", "Claude Haiku 5.5", 1102, 1503, ["30/30 correct", "$0.0016 for 30", "no probability to score"]),
  ("opus",  "Claude Opus 5.5",  1238, 3271, ["30/30 correct", "$0.11 for 30", "no probability to score"]),
] %}
{%- set px = 900 / (rows | map(attribute=3) | max) %}
{%- call content_slide("Decision models") %}
  {{ _STYLE }}
  {{ slide_heading("", "Decision Models") }}
  <svg class="dms" viewBox="0 0 1400 330" role="img"
       aria-label="Median latency per decision on the same 30 tickets: {% for cls, name, p50, p95, facts in rows %}{{ name }} {{ '{:,}'.format(p50) }} ms{{ ', ' if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}. Pale extensions show the 95th percentile.">
    {%- for cls, name, p50, p95, facts in rows %}
    {%- set y = 16 + loop.index0 * 104 %}
    <text x="0" y="{{ y + 42 }}">{{ name }}</text>
    <rect class="{{ cls }} p95" x="340" y="{{ y + 10 }}" width="{{ (p95 * px) | round(1) }}" height="48" rx="8"/>
    <rect class="{{ cls }}" x="340" y="{{ y + 10 }}" width="{{ (p50 * px) | round(1) }}" height="48" rx="8"/>
    <text class="ms" x="{{ 340 + (p95 * px) | round(1) + 16 }}" y="{{ y + 42 }}">{{ "{:,}".format(p50) }} ms</text>
    <text class="sub" x="340" y="{{ y + 86 }}">{% for f in facts %}{{ f }}{% if not loop.last %} <tspan class="sep">&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;</tspan> {% endif %}{% endfor %}</text>
    {%- endfor %}
    <line class="axis" x1="340" y1="0" x2="340" y2="316"/>
    <text class="legend" x="1400" y="326" text-anchor="end">solid bar: median &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; pale bar: 95th percentile</text>
  </svg>
  <p class="dm-src">Jev and Haiku: Zenable decision-models lab, October 2026 (Haiku via OpenRouter, reasoning off). Opus 5.5: the same 30 tickets and prompt through the Claude API on 27 October 2026, effort low; Haiku re-run the same way came in at 1,260 ms median.</p>
{%- endcall %}
{%- endmacro -%}
